```{r, include = FALSE}
knitr::opts_chunk$set(
  collapse = TRUE,
  comment = "#>"
)
```

Confidence intervals for
semipartial correlations,
squared partial correlations,
the improvement in R-squared,
and Cohen's f-squared
are generated using
the `SCorSandwich()`, `PCorSandwich()`, `DeltaRSqSandwich()`,
and `FSqSandwich()` functions from the `betaSandwich` package.
In this example,
we use the data set and the model used in
[betaSandwich: Example Using the BetaHC Function](example-beta-sandwich.html).

```{r}
#| message = FALSE
library(betaSandwich)
```

```{r}
#| echo = FALSE
if (!exists("nas1982")) {
  try(
    data(
      "nas1982",
      package = "betaSandwich"
    ),
    silent = TRUE
  )
}
df <- nas1982
```

```{r}
#| eval = FALSE
df <- betaSandwich::nas1982
```

## Fit the regression model using the `lm()` function.

```{r}
object <- lm(QUALITY ~ NARTIC + PCTGRT + PCTSUPP, data = df)
```

## Estimate the standardized regression slopes and the corresponding sampling covariance matrix.

#### Multivariate Normal-Theory Approach

```{r}
std_mvn <- BetaN(object)
```

#### Asymptotic Distribution-Free Approach

```{r}
std_adf <- BetaADF(object)
```

#### HC3

```{r}
std_hc3 <- BetaHC(object, type = "hc3")
```

## Semipartial correlations

```{r}
summary(SCorSandwich(std_hc3, alpha = 0.05))
```

## Squared partial correlations

```{r}
summary(PCorSandwich(std_hc3, alpha = 0.05))
```

## Improvement in R-squared

```{r}
summary(DeltaRSqSandwich(std_hc3, alpha = 0.05))
```

## Cohen's f-squared and local f-squared

```{r}
summary(FSqSandwich(std_hc3, alpha = 0.05))
```

## Comparing covariance estimators

```{r}
confint(DeltaRSqSandwich(std_mvn), level = 0.95)
confint(DeltaRSqSandwich(std_adf), level = 0.95)
confint(DeltaRSqSandwich(std_hc3), level = 0.95)
```

